> And what, exactly, is ADOM's way of handling this?

As far as I recall...

Moving into a closed door will open it automatically (similar to
Nethack's way of attacking a monster by moving onto its square).
If the door is locked and you carry a key you'll automatically
unlock the door before opening. It's just the move command that
does that all, a single keystroke.

And unintentionally opening/unlocking a door is no worse than
unintentionally running into a floating eye. It would also be
possible, and add safety and still enough ergonomy to the door
procedure, to implement that the first move onto a door square
will give the usual "Bump" or "Ouch" (or whatever) and only a
second move will open/unlock the door (that are two keystrokes
instead of more than a dozen; I think I'd like it most that way).

Nevertheless it would be good (if implemented in Nethack) to be
configurable whether auto-unlock or auto-open should be active.

